{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512828-how-populated-is-a-city-how-populated-is-your-city","id":1512828,"title":"How populated is a City? How populated is YOUR City?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-25T23:53:38-07:00","id":1512828,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How populated is a City? How populated is YOUR City?","content":"I'm working on a big crossover setting filled with nearly a hundred NPCs that will never even show up and I'm curious about just how many supernaturals are in a city. Specifically, how many would you assume for your chronicles?<br /> <br /> So far on my list I have<ul><li>Three Bound (two Sin-eaters and one Tyrant)</li> <li>Fourteen Changelings (it ended up being a Changeling game; there are like eight more Changeling NPCs a player created)</li> <li>Six Mages (and a Proximus who thinks he's a superhero)</li> <li>Ten Hunters (and a Slasher)</li> <li>Eight Vampires (and two Ghouls)</li> <li>Three Prometheans</li> <li>Two Demons, a Fractal, and an Angel on the verge of Falling</li> <li>Four Forsaken, Four Pure</li> <li>Two Deviants (though honestly one of them is just Raiden)</li> <li>One Archmage that's just Ms Frizzle as a Timelord</li> <li>Literally Satan?</li> <li>And a handful of other things that have less than a blurb.</li> </ul>None of this is really anything I have to do, I'm just curious. Also like 20 of the 80 spots on my spreadsheet are trans in some way. But really everyone in CofD is trans unless explicitly stated otherwise.<br /> <br /> Specifically, this setting's conceit is that... well, the Rapture happened. <i><b>Something</b></i> has disconnected the city from reality. A lot of people, mostly mundanes, disappeared. And the supernaturals and the people they've rubbed off on in narratively significant ways (feeding on, victimizing, supporting, inducted into the fold, occultists) are all that's left. Which means the Masquerade isn't long for the world either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":".  What are you, a cop? 05-26-2023, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T03:06:17-07:00","id":1512848,"title":"","content":"I'm working on creating New Orleans as a setting so my numbers are for it. It is primarily going to be a Forsaken game. (Having just checked the population of NOLA it is much, much smaller than I thought. My numbers are probably pretty high, per capita.)<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters: 2-3 Krewes. New Orleans is considered one of the most haunted cities in the world. Probably 10-15 total.<br /> <br /> Forsaken: 4-5 packs and 1 pack of pure. One of my themes though is not having enough Forsaken to adequately handle the city. Probably roughly 20 - 30 total.<br /> <br /> Vampires: Unknown. I'm not comfortable enough with Requiem to narrow it down much. Probably equal to Forsaken at least.<br /> <br /> Changeling: Unknown. Same reason as Vampire. Probably less than Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Gifted Mortals: A lot. I'm not using Mage so this is going to be everything from Catholic priests doing miracles to Voodouns.<br /> <br /> Demons: A small handful, but in deep cover and unlikely to impact the game much.<br /> <br /> Deviants: I don't know, I'm not going to have any kind of Deviant society so they will basically come up randomly in small numbers.<br /> <br /> Prometheans, Mummies, and Beasts: If they exist at all none are known to be in the city on a permanent basis.<br /> <br /> ETA2: Having looked up older threads on this topic I found what people were listing as official numbers from first edition. The Forsaken had roughly half a million world wide and vampires had roughly 1:500,000 mortal ratio so many times less than the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 05-26-2023, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T07:40:43-07:00","id":1512867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512828-how-populated-is-a-city-how-populated-is-your-city?p=1512848#post1512848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on creating New Orleans as a setting so my numbers are for it. It is primarily going to be a Forsaken game. (Having just checked the population of NOLA it is much, much smaller than I thought. My numbers are probably pretty high, per capita.)<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters: 2-3 Krewes. New Orleans is considered one of the most haunted cities in the world. Probably 10-15 total.<br /> <br /> Forsaken: 4-5 packs and 1 pack of pure. One of my themes though is not having enough Forsaken to adequately handle the city. Probably roughly 20 - 30 total.<br /> <br /> Vampires: Unknown. I'm not comfortable enough with Requiem to narrow it down much. Probably equal to Forsaken at least.<br /> <br /> Changeling: Unknown. Same reason as Vampire. Probably less than Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Gifted Mortals: A lot. I'm not using Mage so this is going to be everything from Catholic priests doing miracles to Voodouns.<br /> <br /> Demons: A small handful, but in deep cover and unlikely to impact the game much.<br /> <br /> Deviants: I don't know, I'm not going to have any kind of Deviant society so they will basically come up randomly in small numbers.<br /> <br /> Prometheans, Mummies, and Beasts: If they exist at all none are known to be in the city on a permanent basis.<br /> <br /> ETA2: Having looked up older threads on this topic I found what people were listing as official numbers from first edition. The Forsaken had roughly half a million world wide and vampires had roughly 1:500,000 mortal ratio so many times less than the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that the vampire population is skewed in favor of cities and 1:500,000 just represents the world population. A lot of people live in the wilderness or in the countryside, but those areas don't have as much concentrated human population, and thus not much food for vampires. Basically, cities are where the food it. That ratio is much more narrow when you get inside cities. So, it wouldn't be surprising if there were as many if not more vampires as there are werewolves in New Orleans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T07:40:44-07:00","id":1512868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512828-how-populated-is-a-city-how-populated-is-your-city?p=1512848#post1512848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ETA2: Having looked up older threads on this topic I found what people were listing as official numbers from first edition. The Forsaken had roughly half a million world wide and vampires had roughly 1:500,000 mortal ratio so many times less than the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ratio for vampires can actually be quite varied from place to place, what in itself results in all kinds of dynamics - it could go from anywhere between the 1:500,000 to 1:20,000 mortal ratio, with somewhere between 1:100,000 to 1:50,000 being the most common estimates, according to the 1st edition Requiem corebook itself.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T08:01:35-07:00","id":1512870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1512828-how-populated-is-a-city-how-populated-is-your-city?p=1512867#post1512867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It should be noted that the vampire population is skewed in favor of cities and 1:500,000 just represents the world population. A lot of people live in the wilderness or in the countryside, but those areas don't have as much concentrated human population, and thus not much food for vampires. Basically, cities are where the food it. That ratio is much more narrow when you get inside cities. So, it wouldn't be surprising if there were as many if not more vampires as there are werewolves in New Orleans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise the Uratha tend to favor the wilderness and books discuss the difficulties in getting enough werewolves to cover urban population centers which also tilts the numbers in NOLA towards vampires and away from the Forsaken even more. Then there's the fact that a huge transient population makes wonderful cover for vampires, which is one of the reasons NOLA was the flagship city for Requiem. I could probably go significantly higher on my number of vampires, but it's a werewolf game, I don't figure the exact number of vampires are as important as knowing the general range, just so the werewolves know they can't push the vampires around by strength of numbers alone. <br /> <br /> I just found the old numbers interesting. But I also can't swear to their accuracy, I didn't play first edition, those were just the numbers I found quoted on these boards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T10:38:12-07:00","id":1512978,"title":"","content":"Off and on, I'm working on my fictional city of Buena Vista, Texas, and trying to restrain myself from throwing in the kitchen sink. I intend to make a setting book, and don't want to expect the readers to own the whole library of game lines. Most of the non-Changeling, non-core CoD stuff will mostly be hinted at or use simplified mechanics in the book, but I will go hog wild if I run another game of my own.<ul><li><b>Changelings:</b> The Silver Spire, a massive freehold with nearly 200 members. The city is a hotspot of fae activity and considered part of the battleground in a True Fae feud, with the high number of changelings as one of the results. There is some tension in the freehold: A subgroup calling themselves the Dawn Initiative and a rival Dusk Watch may end up splitting off from the Seasonal Courts to form their own freehold.</li> <li><b>Mummies and their cults:</b> The city once went into a major redesign as a &quot;city of tomorrow&quot; under the guiding hand of a Geomancer, who is now dormant and awaiting a Rite of Return. Players are more likely to deal with her cult, who have a hand in controlling the city council to preserve the city's Sacred Geometry and acquire Relics. Another cult called the Archive, operating out of the Library of Congress in Washington, DC, sends its field agents to Buena Vista to monitor and collect rare and occult texts.</li> <li><b>Hunters:</b> A Union cell operates out of the nearby city of Victoria. The Silver Spire has made diplomatic overtures in hopes of forming an alliance with them, but mutual distrust makes it slow going. The Autumn Court and the Union do share some information about regional threats and are hoping to get a joint operation going to deal with &quot;the Megatoad,&quot; a Spirit-Claimed living in the Mad Island Wetland Management Area. Additionally, a spike in spiritual activity has attracted the attention of Les Mysteries, who are investigating.</li> <li><b>Werewolves:</b> Currently none, and the city may need some Forsaken to address the mentioned spike in spiritual activity.</li> <li><b>Vampires:</b> A few isolated individuals. The Silver Spire is in something of a standoff with a group of Invictus from San Antonio over an incident of human trafficking through BV's ports, souring most of the freehold about vampires. The Summer Court is particularly strident about keeping vampires out of the city. For the time being, the Invictus and Silver Spire avoid each other's territory.</li> <li><b>Mages:</b> There's at least one cabal of mages that managed to remain hidden despite the Autumn and Winter Court's efforts to catalog everything supernatural in the city. It was only the discovery of a deceased Mage's study by one of the newer members that revealed their presence.</li> <li><b>Prometheans:</b> None currently in Buena Vista, though I did have a troupe travel to Philadelphia, where one of them unwittingly encountered the Centimani Oleg Chernenko.</li> <li><b>Sin-Eaters:</b> Thinking about it. I do have a few ideas about using the Underworld.</li> <li><b>Demons:</b> If there are Unchained in BV, they've maintained their Cover quite well.</li> <li><b>Beasts:</b> There's one known Begotten in BV, the young Jane Hardy, who struggles to aim her Hunger for ruin toward positive ends. She's currently working with the Dawn Initiative and has particular interest in taking down wealthy individuals who run their businesses in corrupt or predatory manner.</li> <li><b>Deviants:</b> The Archive uses Ritual Sorcery to imbue their field agents with temporary supernatural powers. In one case, a ritual went too well, transforming one member into a Devoted who can now conjure fictional characters for use in the field. There's also a Renegade artist in town who resulted from an incomplete Claiming by a void spirit.</li> <li><b>Angels of the God-Machine:</b> After someone sabotaged a sizable amount of Infrastructure in Buena Vista, the God-Machine has stepped up construction. It recently finished the Byrne Towers skyscrapers, which host a number of computer and technology companies. An Analyst angel gathers data from these about the city's inhabitants in hopes of finding the saboteurs, believing them to be fae. The Towers' original purpose was an Occult Matrix to allow local Angels to see through The Mask, but the Silver Spire succeeded in destroying the quantum computer that served as its Linchpin. The Silver Spire has warned its members to be very, very careful about what they talk about on social media.</li> <li><b>Spirits:</b> The Autumn Court believes the local Gauntlet has gotten thinner, and with it, more spirits are crossing over and messing with mortals. An incident involving some spiritual seekers looking to get in touch with their &quot;spirit animal&quot; ended up producing the Megatoad. Another active spirit is one of transformation named Skin Giver, who is eager to share the secrets of Skin-Changing with mortals in the city. On the more subtle end, a group of conceptual spirits are inspiring artists with the Implant Mission Numen to make and donate art to the local Museum of Modern Art and shift the site's resonance to their liking. At least one of the museum's curators has noticed there's a strange &quot;art fight&quot; going on between the donors.</li> <li><b>Ghosts:</b> Haven't put much thought into specifics, other than La Llorona making an occasional appearance, wandering the Gulf Coast, looking for her drowned children. The Autumn Court does know the exact method to summon the Geist of Bloody Mary and keeps a tight lid on the secret.</li> <li><b>Genius: The Transgression:</b> One Genius calling himself Dr. Prometheus operates in one of the local Goblin Markets, extolling his vision of a future where people are not bound by their biology. He experiments with splicing together animal traits. One of his Wonders is a &quot;monkey belt&quot; that enhances the wearer, so most people have assumed he's just a particularly eccentric hobgoblin or beast-seeming changeling. For now, he mostly offers alterations and enhancements to one's mien to secure funding and materials for his bigger experiments.</li> <li><b>Mortal Occultists:</b> There are a number of small-time dabblers who stumble on the real thing. A piece of the tourism district affectionately called the Wizard's Quarter deals in occult paraphernalia, and if one knows how to look, books with a variety of Open Rites can be found. One new book making the rounds is The Amateur Exorcist's Emergency Handbook, which contains a crash course in Abjuration, Exorcism, and Warding. I intend to include a few Open Rites of my own design in the setting book that almost anyone with the Occult skill can use, like Fortune Telling and Dowsing.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T22:43:46-07:00","id":1513042,"title":"","content":"I have a file I've been working on setting up Birmingham, AL, as a crossover setting for CtL and DtD. Because of the two games the setting is meant to intersect with, the city is assumed to have a disproportionately high number of changelings and demons, and I have brief write-ups for a few members of each seasonal court and some more established members of the local agency. Besides that, I have two prominent angels, some cryptids typical of the region, a few hunters, some local ghosts, and I haven't settled on their nature for sure, but I imagine around twelve vampires in the metro area, most likely including a couple exiles from larger domains in Atlanta and Nashville.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27841-haintbleu","name":"HaintBleu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T16:03:44-07:00","id":1513339,"title":"","content":"I've been wanting to do a project where I go through all the suggested methods of character/player group/setting creation rules in 2e, set them all in the same city and see how big and messy the city gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T10:58:35-07:00","id":1513793,"title":"","content":"Currently in our city we have the following.<br /> <br /> Mages: A couple hundred that reside in the city proper and a handful in the nearby towns with a couple dozen that are Adept or Master level.<br /> <br /> Changelings: At best there is at best a hundred with a strong concentration of Darklings &amp; Beasts.<br /> <br /> Vampires: There the smallest in number with at best with 2 dozen or so that are barely reached elder status and led by a Carthian Prince.<br /> <br /> Werewolves: There the dominate group in our city and get along best with the Changelings.<br /> <br /> Promtheans: At any given time, you would be lucky to see one of them.<br /> <br /> Immortals of some sort: There was a Purified who resides there at some point, but he hasn't been seen in some time.<br /> <br /> Any others that are haunt the world of darkness don\u2019t have much of a presence in the city and only stay for a very short period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-04-2023, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}